OL,3,AMicrosoft 'deeply sorry' for global
OL,4,Aoutage after almost 24 hours of
OL,5,Adisruption
OL,6,
OL,7,FMicrosoft has said it is "deeply sorry"
OL,8,Ffor the service outage to its products,
OL,9,Fincluding Outlook and Teams, which has
OL,10,Fcaused disruption around the world.
OL,12,FServices were broadly recovering by
OL,13,FFriday afternoon, nearly 24 hours after
OL,14,Fissues first began, as Microsoft said
OL,15,Fit was making "encouraging progress"
OL,16,Fand email queues were nearing normal
OL,17,Flevels.
OL,23,APub: 13-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBTechnologyC Nat RadioFCulture
FL,107,105,200,160,0,100
PN,10602
